[36m(TaskRunner pid=1199197)[0m Each additional line will cross all previous lines because it connects two points in different quadrants. The maximum number of intersections of \( n \) lines is given by the combination formula \( \binom{n}{2} \), which calculates the number of unique pairs of lines. So, for 25 additional lines, the number of intersections is:
