[36m(TaskRunner pid=1199197)[0m ### Step 2: Modeling the Problem
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1199197)[0m We can model this problem by considering the gaps between the people. Since no two people can sit next to each other, we need to place 8 people with at least one empty chair between each pair. This means we need at least 7 empty chairs (one between each pair of people) and the remaining 9 chairs can be distributed freely among the 9 gaps (7 between people and 2 at the ends).
