[36m(TaskRunner pid=1199197)[0m We start by considering the Fermat point (or Torricelli point) for the triangles \( ABD \) and \( ACE \) since these triangles share the angles \( \angle B = 60^\circ \) and \( \angle E = 60^\circ \).
