[36m(TaskRunner pid=1199197)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1199197)[0m ### Step 2: Use a Recursive Approach
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1199197)[0m Let's define \(a_n\) as the number of ways to place \(n\) people in \(n+1\) chairs such that no two people sit next to each other. The sequence will start with an "E" or end with an "E", so we can use the following recurrence relation:
