[36m(TaskRunner pid=1199197)[0m A known result in geometry is that the point that minimizes the sum of distances to the vertices of a convex polygon with a \( 120^\circ \) angle is a special point related to the circumcircle of the polygon. However, for this problem, we can use the known result that the minimum sum of distances for a pentagon with the given properties can be calculated directly.
